00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.260
And so like, you know, they find ways to up the stakes here.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:56.120
And in addition to the kicks, there is also the sparks, which are like, they patrol the border of first the square, but then eventually you're, you know, filled in areas too.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:07:03.260
So that you have to also not just be like hugging the walls while you anticipate the kicks moving away.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:13.940
You have to kind of continuously dodge both, you know, your, your created space and the, the void space that you're trying to fill.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:19.600
All the while you have two options of speed to fill in.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:23.740
And at first I just couldn't figure out a reason for why you would ever use the slow one.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.680
There's a slow speed and a faster speed.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.500
The slower speed rewards more points.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:34.140
So if you don't care about points, then have I got great news for you.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:42.600
There's an easier version of this game, but if you do care about the points, you know, you'll, you'll use the slower one in order to accumulate more points.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.740
Granted, you'll be filling in the screen a little slower.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:08:04.160
I think the game itself, even though kicks feels like it moves randomly, does have kicks be way more forgiving at the beginning of the game in the way that like when you're playing it, you feel like you can start by just filling in like at least 40%, if not more of the screen on the first stage.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:12.640
Yeah. That is a behavior that is bad to take with you throughout the game because you will be punished for trying to make giant spaces.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:24.800
And it looks like really good players just focus on making like very small, like two to 5% clears at a time before they go back to their larger area.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:31.880
Because you want to just continue to confine the space that kicks is in rather than try to make one big pull.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.980
You're not rewarded necessarily for your speed.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:46.280
Yeah. And I, and I, I do think that in the first, at least the first level, I think the kicks AI is actually designed to avoid contact with you.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.700
