00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:44.240
I think it makes sense where if you're filling a space, you know, and it's like your space is, the space is, the void at first is large.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:51.200
And as you fill it in, it gets smaller, but so is the, you know, you're now confining the kicks to a smaller area too.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.780
So as it's moving around, you have more chance to make contact with it.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.420
Because the kicks can't pass by anything you've drawn.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:01.960
