00:37:20.680 --> 00:37:22.460
And it's like, yeah, it's interesting.

00:37:22.820 --> 00:37:29.040
Like, they do evolve it enough, but they keep the, the vibe, they keep the, the core there.

00:37:29.480 --> 00:37:33.180
Yeah. So I definitely want to check this out after checking all this out.

00:37:33.280 --> 00:37:35.860
Oh, and it's interesting too, because of watching it.

00:37:35.980 --> 00:37:41.420
Like, they really make, the animation makes it look like you're cutting something away.

00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:44.960
Yeah, so maybe we're the antagonist.

00:37:45.180 --> 00:37:48.080
Yeah, yeah. Maybe Kicks is just trying to live its life.

00:37:48.080 --> 00:37:50.960
Oh, I thought maybe we're cutting away like a virus or something.

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:52.220
Oh, okay.

00:37:52.300 --> 00:37:55.380
Something bad. Yeah, so Kicks again is the antagonist.

00:37:55.480 --> 00:37:59.180
Thank goodness. I couldn't, I couldn't live with myself if it was me.

00:37:59.560 --> 00:38:06.220
Right. But I also couldn't live with myself if we didn't do the Essential Games List.

00:38:09.700 --> 00:38:11.620
Joe. You know what?

00:38:11.720 --> 00:38:14.700
I'm tempted to throw this a vote.

00:38:14.700 --> 00:38:21.420
But what stops me is actually a conversation we had on our Best of 90 episode when I brought up To the Earth.

00:38:21.820 --> 00:38:29.780
And you guys kind of mentioned to me, like, I think To the Earth for you, Joe, is just kind of like scratching an itch for you that you really, really like.

00:38:29.880 --> 00:38:31.160
And I think that's true.

00:38:32.060 --> 00:38:33.780
And I think it's true for Kicks, too.

00:38:33.860 --> 00:38:39.880
Where I'm like, I think it's just like, it scratches my brain in a way where I'm like, oh, this is like, I really like this.

00:38:39.880 --> 00:38:43.000
And I think people who like this kind of game definitely give it a try.

00:38:43.340 --> 00:38:45.300
I don't know if I could say it's essential.

00:38:45.560 --> 00:38:51.860
Like, I don't know if it's, if it's, if it's going to be widespread beloved enough to be essential.

00:38:51.860 --> 00:38:55.700
I'm not even sure I'm going to love it as much as I do right now with the recency bias I have.

00:38:55.780 --> 00:38:57.320
But I was just like, oh, this is really cool.

00:38:57.420 --> 00:39:00.240
And I kind of got a little addicted to it for a little bit while I was playing it.

00:39:01.120 --> 00:39:04.240
But I think it's a definite play, especially if you're like this kind of game.

00:39:04.320 --> 00:39:07.640
But I don't know if I can go as far as to say it's an essential game.

00:39:07.980 --> 00:39:11.580
Yeah. It's a really smart game.

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:20.520
It's, it's a, it's a, it's somehow an early arcade game that, while it did obviously get clones, we talked about quite a few of them.

00:39:20.780 --> 00:39:24.400
It didn't go into anybody else's lane at the time.

00:39:24.940 --> 00:39:36.120
And, and not too many things like iterate on this idea of like filling the void in a satisfying way while also having a terrifying enemy.

00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:39.780
You know, there's, there is no ending in Kicks.

00:39:39.880 --> 00:39:40.940
There's no final boss.

00:39:40.940 --> 00:39:42.120
There's no credit roll.

00:39:42.280 --> 00:39:44.720
There's no conclusion. You, you just play until you die.

00:39:44.860 --> 00:39:46.840
And the whole point is for a high score.

00:39:47.580 --> 00:39:56.640
And video games today, most, I would say like 95% of video games today, narrative completion is table stakes.

00:39:56.640 --> 00:40:00.980
Like most people play a game and they want to just see the credits roll.

00:40:01.100 --> 00:40:03.800
And that's how they define beating a video game.

00:40:04.380 --> 00:40:20.300
Is there, is there still room for a game like Kicks that presumably, you know, nobody will, nobody will be able to claim that they perfected it, but also nobody will, not too many people will be able to even just clear the levels that are within the game itself.

00:40:20.300 --> 00:40:22.500
Is there still room for something like that?

00:40:23.340 --> 00:40:24.620
I think so.

00:40:25.040 --> 00:40:38.380
And I think it's the same reason why I like, why I like all these arcade games that, that didn't have things that iterated on them or like that started something.

00:40:38.380 --> 00:40:41.800
It was like, the, the fun is just that it's a pure video game.

00:40:41.980 --> 00:40:48.620
You know, you're just like, all I'm doing is just filling in lines and there's no like, there's no special trick moves.

00:40:48.860 --> 00:40:54.320
There's no like, uh, you know, street fighter two quarter circle this and input these options.

00:40:54.620 --> 00:41:02.000
There's, it's always just like, do the, do the two instructions and you can pick up and play this game whenever you want.

00:41:02.120 --> 00:41:04.960
It reminds me of how I feel about Jairus in that way.

00:41:04.960 --> 00:41:08.360
And Jairus, I try to get on the essential games list several times.

00:41:10.580 --> 00:41:21.160
Uh, and I think like that it's for the same reason that when we talked about Shadowgate and stuff like that, like it's okay that they're not necessarily the best version, but that they should still be on the essential games list.

00:41:21.340 --> 00:41:24.360
It does make me want to put kicks on the essential games list.

00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:32.800
Cause I think if it isn't just open up to like the NES version, which to me, by all means seems superior than the arcade version I, I haven't played.

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:34.680
I do think that this is great.

00:41:34.940 --> 00:41:36.300
Is there room for improvement?

00:41:36.860 --> 00:41:40.100
Like multiplayer having co-op and the power up stuff?

00:41:40.300 --> 00:41:44.360
Sure. But like the game they put here has very little to actually critique.

00:41:44.640 --> 00:41:46.180
It just makes you want more of it.

00:41:46.280 --> 00:41:47.820
And so I think that's a pretty good sign.

00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:50.940
So I am going to vote it on the essential games list.

00:41:51.060 --> 00:41:57.180
But unfortunately, since there's only two of us, that means that it will not get on because we always, you always need more than half.

00:41:57.180 --> 00:41:58.860
And so 50% of the vote.

00:41:59.200 --> 00:42:05.620
We need, we need Sean now in the best of 91 in like two and a half years to break the tie.

00:42:06.020 --> 00:42:11.820
But see now it's a bummer that it has to be a unanimous vote in the best of 91.

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:17.160
Right. Not that I will, like I'm so opposed to ever changing my vote on this one, but it's like,

00:42:17.220 --> 00:42:22.540
I would like to know where Sean would have voted to see if it would have gotten on or not before the best of.

00:42:23.160 --> 00:42:26.220
Oh, and you know, we don't have that long till the best of 91.

00:42:26.640 --> 00:42:29.500
We just have to wait until March of 2028.

00:42:29.840 --> 00:42:31.020
So plenty of time.

00:42:31.200 --> 00:42:33.440
Yeah. We'll be able to figure it all out by then.

00:42:33.840 --> 00:42:38.800
I'm sure you and Sean will be playing it every week until then to make sure that your taste is at the same time.

00:42:38.800 --> 00:42:39.760
Stay fresh on it. Yeah.

00:42:40.340 --> 00:42:44.120
Yep. Now next week we will be playing The Untouchables.

00:42:47.260 --> 00:42:48.760
Can you, can you touch this?

00:42:50.500 --> 00:42:51.800
The only one way to find out.

00:42:52.540 --> 00:42:54.560
The Untouchables.
